    intro: [
      T('许多原子核有自旋，像一个小磁针。把它放进磁场 B₀，自旋的能量分裂成几个能级（Zeeman 分裂），核磁矩绕磁场以 Larmor 频率进动：¹H 在 9.4 T 下是 400 MHz，落在射频波段。用同样频率的射频脉冲去“推”这些自旋，它们就一起偏离磁场方向，随后的进动在线圈里感应出一个微弱的电压。这就是 NMR 信号。',
        'Many nuclei have spin and behave like tiny bar magnets. In a magnetic field B₀ the spin energy splits into a few levels (the Zeeman splitting) and the nuclear moment precesses about the field at the Larmor frequency: 400 MHz for ¹H at 9.4 T, in the radio-frequency band. A radio-frequency pulse at that frequency tips the spins away from the field together, and their precession then induces a faint voltage in a coil. That voltage is the NMR signal.'),
      T('NMR 之所以对化学有用，是因为这个频率会被周围的电子微微改变。电子屏蔽磁场，让不同化学环境里的同一种核频率相差百万分之几（化学位移）；通过化学键相连的核互相分裂对方的谱线（J 耦合）；空间上靠近的核通过偶极相互作用交换磁化（NOE）；自旋回到平衡的快慢（弛豫）反映分子怎样运动。一张谱里同时装着连接关系、距离、角度和动力学。',
        'NMR is useful to chemistry because that frequency is shifted slightly by the surrounding electrons. Electrons shield the field, so the same kind of nucleus in different chemical environments differs by parts per million (the chemical shift); nuclei connected through bonds split each other\'s lines (J coupling); nuclei close in space exchange magnetisation through the dipolar interaction (the NOE); and how fast the spins return to equilibrium (relaxation) reports on molecular motion. One spectrum carries connectivity, distances, angles and dynamics at once.'),
      T('NMR 的弱点是灵敏度。室温下，9.4 T 磁场里每十万个 ¹H 中只有大约三个的净取向贡献信号。八十多年来方法发展的一大半，都可以看成在同这个弱点较量：更强的磁场、傅里叶变换、极化转移、低温探头、超极化，以及完全不靠线圈的新探测方式。另一半则是在想办法把越来越复杂的谱拆开：多维谱、同位素标记、魔角旋转、TROSY、非均匀采样和机器学习。',
        'The weakness of NMR is sensitivity. At room temperature in a 9.4 T magnet, only about three in every hundred thousand ¹H spins contribute net signal. More than half of eighty years of method development can be read as a fight against this weakness: stronger magnets, the Fourier transform, polarisation transfer, cryogenic probes, hyperpolarisation, and new detectors that do without a coil. The other half is about pulling apart ever more crowded spectra: multidimensional NMR, isotope labelling, magic-angle spinning, TROSY, non-uniform sampling and machine learning.'),
    ],

